{"nodes": [{"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_02_routing_and_navigation_07d_what_the_matcher_silently_skips_md", "label": "07d-what-the-matcher-silently-skips.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/02-routing-and-navigation/07d-what-the-matcher-silently-skips.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "A Server Function is not a route in the matching chain but a POST to whichever route imported it, so excluding a path also excludes every Server Function called from it \u2014 and _next/data runs your proxy even when you exclude it, because Next.js decided that particular hole was too dangerous to let you dig", "sidebar_label": "07d \u00b7 What the matcher skips", "sidebar_position": "41", "description": "The Server-Function POST trap that silently removes auth coverage and survives refactors, the deliberate _next/data override of your own configuration, why prefetch requests run proxy too and what that costs, and asserting matcher coverage in a unit test with unstable_doesProxyMatch."}}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_02_routing_and_navigation_07d_what_the_matcher_silently_skips_next_data_ignores_your_exclusion_on_purpose", "label": "\ud83d\udd34 `_next/data` ignores your exclusion, on purpose", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/02-routing-and-navigation/07d-what-the-matcher-silently-skips.md", "source_location": "L15"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_02_routing_and_navigation_07d_what_the_matcher_silently_skips_the_server_function_trap", "label": "\ud83d\udd34 The Server Function trap", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/02-routing-and-navigation/07d-what-the-matcher-silently-skips.md", "source_location": "L30"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_02_routing_and_navigation_07d_what_the_matcher_silently_skips_prefetch_requests_run_proxy_too", "label": "Prefetch requests run proxy